  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Fluorine does not form oxyacids as it is the most electronegative&nbsp; However, at <math><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mn>40</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> it forms HOF. (Unstable at room temperature). Chlorine forms four types of oxyacids. Sulphur forms many oxy acids. Nitrogen mainly forms two types of oxyacids.</p></blockquote>"
